<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<RunSettings>
  <RunConfiguration>
    <!--
      A WALL-CLOCK CAP ON THE WHOLE SESSION - not a connection timeout.

      The comment that stood here said this "prevents vstest from timing out on
      first connection" and pointed at VSTEST_CONNECTION_TIMEOUT. That is a
      different setting, and believing this one was about connecting is why
      nobody looked at it while it was cutting real runs short.
      TestSessionTimeout kills the run when the clock runs out, and fifteen
      minutes could not finish EITHER leg of this project:

          net9.0,  quiet box         14 m 46 s
          net10.0, quiet box         20 m 11 s
          net9.0,  box under load    28 m 05 s

      So the command CLAUDE.md documents aborted at minute fifteen and printed
      "Failed!" with about 54 tests never run - which reads exactly like a real
      break, and cost most of 2026-10-24 before the cap was found rather than
      the suite blamed.

      Forty-five minutes is 1.6x the worst run measured here. The cap is there
      to stop a HUNG run holding the box overnight; it is not a judgement on how
      fast this suite ought to be. Raise it again rather than trimming tests to
      fit it - and if it ever trips, read it as "something is stuck", because
      nothing healthy here takes that long.
    -->
    <TestSessionTimeout>2700000</TestSessionTimeout>
  </RunConfiguration>
</RunSettings>
